## 3. Create new `HeadingActionsMenu.vue` component:

```vue src/components/HeadingActionsMenu.vue
<script setup>
</script>

<template>
  <div 
    class="absolute -right-20 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 flex gap-1 z-50 pointer-events-auto"
    @mouseenter="onMouseEnter"
    @mouseleave="onMouseLeave"
  >
    <button
      class="btn btn-xs btn-ghost tooltip tooltip-left"
      data-tip="Copy chapter"
      @click="handleCopyChapter"
      title="Copy this chapter and all content until the next heading of same level"
    >
      <i class="fa-solid fa-copy text-primary"></i>
    </button>
    <button
      class="btn btn-xs btn-ghost tooltip tooltip-left"
      data-tip="Create task"
      @click="handleCreateTask"
      title="Create a task from this chapter"
    >
      <i class="fa-solid fa-tasks text-warning"></i>
    </button>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: {
    headingId: { type: String, required: true },
    headingLevel: { type: Number, required: true },
    documentId: { type: String, required: true },
    fullContent: { type: String, required: true }
  },
  emits: ['copy-chapter', 'create-task'],
  data() {
    return {
      isHovered: false
    }
  },
  methods: {
    extractChapterContent() {
      const lines = this.fullContent.split('\n')
      const startLineIndex = this.findHeadingLineIndex(lines)

      if (startLineIndex === -1) return ''

      let endLineIndex = lines.length

      // Find next heading of same or higher level
      for (let i = startLineIndex + 1; i < lines.length; i++) {
        const match = lines[i].match(/^(#{1,6})\s+/)
        if (match) {
          const level = match[1].length
          if (level <= this.headingLevel) {
            endLineIndex = i
            break
          }
        }
      }

      return lines.slice(startLineIndex, endLineIndex).join('\n')
    },
    findHeadingLineIndex(lines) {
      // Extract heading text from ID
      const headingText = this.headingId
        .replace(this.documentId + '-', '')
        .replace(/-/g, ' ')

      for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
        const match = lines[i].match(/^(#{1,6})\s+(.+)$/)
        if (match) {
          const lineText = match[2]
            .toLowerCase()
            .replace(/[^\w\s-]/g, '')
            .trim()
            .replace(/\s+/g, '-')

          if (lineText === headingText) {
            return i
          }
        }
      }
      return -1
    },
    getHeadingText(lines, lineIndex) {
      const match = lines[lineIndex].match(/^(#{1,6})\s+(.+)$/)
      return match ? match[2] : 'Chapter'
    },
    handleCopyChapter() {
      const chapterContent = this.extractChapterContent()
      const lines = this.fullContent.split('\n')
      const startLineIndex = this.findHeadingLineIndex(lines)
      const headingText = this.getHeadingText(lines, startLineIndex)

      this.$emit('copy-chapter', {
        headingId: this.headingId,
        headingText,
        headingLevel: this.headingLevel,
        content: chapterContent
      })
    },
    handleCreateTask() {
      const chapterContent = this.extractChapterContent()
      const lines = this.fullContent.split('\n')
      const startLineIndex = this.findHeadingLineIndex(lines)
      const headingText = this.getHeadingText(lines, startLineIndex)

      this.$emit('create-task', {
        headingId: this.headingId,
        headingText,
        headingLevel: this.headingLevel,
        content: chapterContent
      })
    },
    onMouseEnter() {
      this.isHovered = true
    },
    onMouseLeave() {
      this.isHovered = false
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

## Summary of Changes

**Key fixes:**

1. **Added `group` class to headings** - Enables the group-based hover styling
2. **Changed event handlers** - `onHeadingHover` now correctly detects heading elements and sets `hoveredHeadingId`
3. **Added `onHeadingLeave`** - Clears the hovered state when mouse leaves
4. **Fixed positioning** - Absolute positioning with `-right-20` places buttons to the right of the heading
5. **Better hover detection** - Uses `event.target.closest()` to find parent heading element
6. **Added transition** - Smooth fade in/out of the action buttons
7. **Split components** - `HeadingActionsMenu.vue` handles the actual menu UI and logic separately

Now when you hover over any H1, H2, or H3 heading, the action buttons (copy and create task) will appear to the right side of the heading!

I'll create a dedicated renderer component for headings similar to the table renderer pattern. This will extract all heading logic from `MarkdownViewer.vue`.

